     ],
     "summary": "names accepts all non-common name terms, or one name term the caller's rare test accepts.",
     "rationale": "The two-term rule in covers passes a test that accepts nothing, so refused payment keeps finding nothing. The anchor check passes rare-and-alone, which keeps long intents such as CI scripts resolve origin/main from the branch ref only. An off-topic intent using one claim's own name term (refund an added item) still names it; docs/word-index.md states that limit.",
     "author": "fm/verilex-false-greens"
    }
